{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator/allocate_bytes","title":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>::allocate_bytes","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator&lt;T&gt;::</span>allocate_bytes","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/allocate_bytes","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"Allocates nbytes bytes of storage at specified alignment alignment using the underlying memory resource. Equivalent to return resource()->allocate(nbytes, alignment);.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> allocate_bytes<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> nbytes,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> alignment <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> alignof<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/max_align_t\"><span class=\"kw111\">std::<span class=\"me2\">max_align_t</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Allocates <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">nbytes</span></code> bytes of storage at specified alignment <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">alignment</span></code> using the underlying memory resource. Equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> resource<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>allocate<span class=\"br0\">(</span>nbytes, alignment<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> nbytes\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the number of bytes to allocate\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> alignment\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the alignment to use\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A pointer to the allocated storage. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function was introduced for use with the fully-specialized allocator <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span></span></code>, but it may be useful in any specialization.\n</p><p>The return type is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span></code> (rather than, e.g., <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/byte\"><span class=\"kw2659\">std::<span class=\"me2\">byte</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span></code>) to support conversion to an arbitrary pointer type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">U<span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span></code> by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">static_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>May throw any exceptions thrown by the call to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">resource<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>allocate</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/allocate_object\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate_object</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocates raw memory suitable for an object or an array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/new_object\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>new_object</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocates and constructs an object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/allocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocate memory <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits/allocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocates uninitialized storage using the allocator <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function of <code>std::allocator_traits&lt;Alloc&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/memory_resource/allocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>allocate</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  allocates memory <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::pmr::memory_resource</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator","title":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>::allocate_bytes","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Allocates nbytes bytes of storage at specified alignment alignment using the underlying memory resource."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"nbytes, alignment"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A pointer to the allocated storage."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function was introduced for use with the fully-specialized allocator std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<>, but it may be useful in any specialization."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw any exceptions thrown by the call to resource()->allocate."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"allocate_object","note":"allocates raw memory suitable for an object or an array"},{"label":"new_object","note":"allocates and constructs an object"},{"label":"allocate","note":"allocate memory"},{"label":"allocate","note":"allocates uninitialized storage using the allocator"},{"label":"allocate","note":"allocates memory"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":156,"codeBlockCount":0}
